r\",\"text\":\"The TheTaxCalc Scholarship is open to U.S. citizens, permanent residents, and visa holders who are currently enrolled at an accredited U.S. college or university (undergraduate or graduate) with at least a 3.0 cumulative GPA. Eligible majors include finance, accounting, economics, taxation, business administration, mathematics, and related fields. High school seniors with proof of enrollment for the upcoming fall semester are also welcome to apply.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much is the scholarship award and when is the deadline?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The 2026 TheTaxCalc Scholarship is a one-time $2,500 award. Applications open January 1, 2026 and the final deadline is May 31, 2026 at 11:59 PM Pacific Time. The winner is announced on or before July 15, 2026. Funds are paid directly to the winner's college or university to be applied toward tuition, fees, or required course materials.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What materials do I need to submit with my application?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You'll need three items: (1) a 500–800 word original essay on how understanding personal taxation improves financial literacy and long-term wealth building, (2) a current resume or CV highlighting your academic and extracurricular activities, and (3) proof of current enrollment (an unofficial transcript or registration confirmation). All materials must be submitted through our online application form by the deadline — emailed or mailed submissions are not accepted.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How is the winner selected and when will I be notified?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Applications are reviewed by a committee of TheTaxCalc editors and a Certified Public Accountant (CPA). Essays are scored on clarity (30%), originality (30%), relevance to modern tax issues (25%), and writing mechanics (15%). Finalists may be contacted for a brief phone interview. The winner is notified by email no later than July 15, 2026 and announced on our blog shortly after. All applicants receive a confirmation email upon submission.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I apply more than once or reapply in future years?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You may submit only one application per cycle. Previous applicants who did not win are welcome to reapply in subsequent years, provided they still meet the eligibility requirements. Previous winners are not eligible to apply again. The TheTaxCalc Scholarship runs annually, so even if you miss this year's deadline you can apply for next year's award.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is there any cost to apply or any obligation if I win?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. The TheTaxCalc Scholarship is 100% free to apply — there is no application fee and no purchase required. If you win, the only obligation is to provide a brief headshot and short quote that we may use in our winner announcement. You retain all rights to your essay. We will never sell your personal information or use your contact details for marketing without explicit opt-in consent.\"}}]},{\"@type\":\"EducationalOccupationalProgram\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc Scholarship 2026\",\"description\":\"A $2,500 scholarship for undergraduate and graduate students studying finance, accounting, economics, or tax.\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com/scholarship\",\"provider\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"TheTaxCalc\",\"url\":\"https://thetaxcalc.com\"},\"offers\":{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"price\":\"2500\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"availability\":\"https://schema.org/InStock\"},\"applicationDeadline\":\"2026-05-31\",\"startDate\":\"2026-01-01\"}]}0:{\"rsc\":[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:px-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$2\"}}],\"$L3\",\"$L4\",\"$L5\",\"$L6\",\"$L7\",\"$L8\",\"$L9\",\"$La\",\"$Lb\"]}],null,\"$Lc\"]}],\"isPartial\":false,\"staleTime\":300,\"varyParams\":null,\"buildId\":\"CoYzXiyUkcJG_1nbCXYOa\"}\n3:[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"mb-6 flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"hover:text-foreground transition-colors\",\"children\":\"Home\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"/\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-foreground font-medium\",\"children\":\"Scholarship\"}]]}]\n4:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-500/20 bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-500/10 to-teal-500/5 p-8 text-center\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-emerald-400 mb-4\",\"children\":\"2026 Application Now Open\"}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-4xl mb-4\",\"children\":\"TheTaxCalc Scholarship — $2,500 Award\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto\",\"children\":\"Supporting the next generation of tax professionals, financial planners, and economists. Open to U.S. undergraduate and graduate students studying finance, accounting, economics, or taxation.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3 text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full bg-background/50 px-3 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Award: \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"$$2,500\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full bg-background/50 px-3 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Deadline: \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground\",\"children\":\"May 31, 2026\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-full bg-background/50 px-3 py-1.5 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[\"Cost: \",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"Free to Apply\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n5:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"About the Scholarship\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"At TheTaxCalc, we believe that understanding taxation is the foundation of financial literacy. Our free tax calculators — covering paycheck estimation, capital gains, self-employment, retirement, and more — have helped millions of Americans better understand where their money goes. The TheTaxCalc Scholarship extends that mission by supporting students who are pursuing careers in finance, accounting, economics, and tax policy.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"The 2026 TheTaxCalc Scholarship is a one-time $2,500 award given to one outstanding student who demonstrates academic excellence, an interest in taxation or personal finance, and a commitment to helping others make better financial decisions. Funds are paid directly to the winner’s accredited U.S. college or university and can be applied toward tuition, fees, or required course materials for the 2026-2027 academic year.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"We launched this scholarship in 2024 as a way to give back to the community that has supported TheTaxCalc since our founding. Past winners have gone on to careers at Big Four accounting firms, regional CPA practices, financial planning firms, and public policy organizations. If you are passionate about helping people understand their taxes and build long-term wealth, we want to hear from you.\"}]]}]\n6:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10 rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Eligibility Requirements\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-2 text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"U.S. citizen, permanent resident, or valid visa holder\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"U.S. citizen, permanent resident, or valid visa holder\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Currently enrolled at an accredited U.S. college or university (undergraduate or graduate)\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Currently enrolled at an accredited U.S. college or university (undergraduate or graduate)\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Cumulative GPA of 3.0 or higher\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Majoring in finance, accounting, economics, taxation, business administration, mathematics, or a closely related field\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Majoring in finance, accounting, economics, taxation, business administration, mathematics, or a closely related field\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"High school seniors with proof of enrollment for the upcoming fall semester are also eligible\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"High school seniors with proof of enrollment for the upcoming fall semester are also eligible\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"At least 17 years old at the time of application\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 mt-0.5\",\"children\":\"✓\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"At least 17 years old at the time of application\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n7:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"How to Apply\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Applications are accepted online only. To apply for the 2026 TheTaxCalc Scholarship, submit the following three items through our online application form by 11:59 PM Pacific Time on May 31, 2026:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"1\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"Original Essay\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A 500–800 word essay on how understanding personal taxation improves financial literacy and long-term wealth building. Must be original and unpublished.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"2\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"Resume / CV\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"A current resume highlighting your academic achievements, extracurricular activities, work experience, and any community involvement.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-400 mb-2\",\"children\":\"3\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-1\",\"children\":\"Proof of Enrollment\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"An unofficial transcript or registration confirmation showing current enrollment at an accredited U.S. institution.\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4\",\"children\":[\"Email submissions are not accepted. To request an application form, contact\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:scholarship@thetaxcalc.com\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"scholarship@thetaxcalc.com\"}],\" \",\"with the subject line “2026 Scholarship Application Request.”\"]}]]}]\n8:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Selection Process\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":\"Applications are reviewed by a committee composed of TheTaxCalc editors and an external Certified Public Accountant (CPA) who volunteers as a reader. Each essay is scored on four criteria, weighted as follows:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Clarity of argument and thesis\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Clarity of argument and thesis\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"30%\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Originality of perspective\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Originality of perspective\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"30%\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Relevance to modern tax issues\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Relevance to modern tax issues\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"25%\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Writing mechanics (grammar, structure, style)\",{\"className\":\"flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Writing mechanics (grammar, structure, style)\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-emerald-400\",\"children\":\"15%\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-4 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Finalists may be contacted for a brief 15-minute phone interview. The winner is notified by email no later than July 15, 2026 and announced on our blog shortly after. All applicants receive a confirmation email upon submission, and finalists who are not selected are notified by August 31, 2026.\"}]]}]\n9:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6\",\"children\":\"Scholarship FAQ\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",\"Who is eligible to apply for the TheTaxCalc Scholarship?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Who is eligible to apply for the TheTaxCalc Scholarship?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The TheTaxCalc Scholarship is open to U.S. citizens, permanent residents, and visa holders who are currently enrolled at an accredited U.S. college or university (undergraduate or graduate) with at least a 3.0 cumulative GPA. Eligible majors include finance, accounting, economics, taxation, business administration, mathematics, and related fields. High school seniors with proof of enrollment for the upcoming fall semester are also welcome to apply.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"How much is the scholarship award and when is the deadline?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"How much is the scholarship award and when is the deadline?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"The 2026 TheTaxCalc Scholarship is a one-time $2,500 award. Applications open January 1, 2026 and the final deadline is May 31, 2026 at 11:59 PM Pacific Time. The winner is announced on or before July 15, 2026. Funds are paid directly to the winner's college or university to be applied toward tuition, fees, or required course materials.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"What materials do I need to submit with my application?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"What materials do I need to submit with my application?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"You'll need three items: (1) a 500–800 word original essay on how understanding personal taxation improves financial literacy and long-term wealth building, (2) a current resume or CV highlighting your academic and extracurricular activities, and (3) proof of current enrollment (an unofficial transcript or registration confirmation). All materials must be submitted through our online application form by the deadline — emailed or mailed submissions are not accepted.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"How is the winner selected and when will I be notified?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"How is the winner selected and when will I be notified?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Applications are reviewed by a committee of TheTaxCalc editors and a Certified Public Accountant (CPA). Essays are scored on clarity (30%), originality (30%), relevance to modern tax issues (25%), and writing mechanics (15%). Finalists may be contacted for a brief phone interview. The winner is notified by email no later than July 15, 2026 and announced on our blog shortly after. All applicants receive a confirmation email upon submission.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",\"Can I apply more than once or reapply in future years?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[\"$Le\",\"$Lf\"]}],\"$L10\"]}]]}]\na:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-10\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold text-foreground mb-4\",\"children\":\"Related Resources\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Ld\",\"/paycheck-calculator\",{\"href\":\"/paycheck-calculator\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Paycheck Calculator\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\",\"children\":\"See how tax brackets work in practice with our free paycheck calculator.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Ld\",\"/methodology\",{\"href\":\"/methodology\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"Tax Calculation Methodology\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\",\"children\":\"Understand exactly how we compute federal, state, and FICA taxes.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Ld\",\"/about\",{\"href\":\"/about\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"About TheTaxCalc\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\",\"children\":\"Learn about our mission to make tax knowledge accessible to everyone.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$Ld\",\"/tax-professionals\",{\"href\":\"/tax-professionals\",\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-4 hover:border-emerald-500/40 hover:bg-emerald-500/5 transition-colors\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium text-foreground\",\"children\":\"For Tax Professionals\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-1\",\"children\":\"Resources and tools for CPAs, EAs, and tax preparers.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\nb:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-xl border border-border/30 bg-muted/10 p-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Official Rules & Terms\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":[\"The TheTaxCalc Scholarship is administered by TheTaxCalc. Employees of TheTaxCalc and their immediate family members are not eligible. The winner consents to the use of their name, headshot, and essay excerpt for promotional purposes. The decision of the selection committee is final. By applying, you agree to the full official rules available at\",\" \",[\"$\",\"$Ld\",null,{\"href\":\"/terms\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"/terms\"}],\". For questions, email\",\" \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"mailto:scholarship@thetaxcalc.com\",\"className\":\"text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 underline\",\"children\":\"scholarship@thetaxcalc.com\"}],\".\"]}]]}]}]\nc:[\"$\",\"$L11\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$12\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@13\"}]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Can I apply more than once or reapply in future years?\"}]\nf:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"You may submit only one application per cycle. Previous applicants who did not win are welcome to reapply in subsequent years, provided they still meet the eligibility requirements. Previous winners are not eligible to apply again. The TheTaxCalc Scholarship runs annually, so even if you miss this year's deadline you can apply for next year's award.\"}]\n10:[\"$\",\"div\",\"Is there any cost to apply or any obligation if I win?\",{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border/30 bg-card/50 p-5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-foreground mb-2\",\"children\":\"Is there any cost to apply or any obligation if I win?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"No. The TheTaxCalc Scholarship is 100% free to apply — there is no application fee and no purchase required. If you win, the only obligation is to provide a brief headshot and short quote t